## What this session did

Implemented the DLM half of GPT's option-D fix for the step-4a mount bootstrap deadlock that sess55 identified and held the rig run over. **Tree is at 0.11.400, srcversion `E734C49BAF50F1E80D9BFC9`, builds clean.**

**The API split** (`dlm/v5_mount.c`, `dlm/v5_mount.h`). `mxfs_v5_dlm_mount_settle` was a single post-`xfs_mountfs` unit; it is now four pieces, with a new shared core `v5_settle_resolve(ctx, dispatch)` doing confirm-dead → fence → note-dead → mark-pending:

- `dispatch=true` — the settle worker's path, elect + notify, async replay.
- `dispatch=false` — the barrier's path: mark recovery pending, no election. The mounting node has to resolve these itself, because its own recovery is precisely what collides with those grants.
- `mxfs_v5_dlm_settle_own_slot` / `_mount_recovery_cohort` / `_mount_cohort_complete` are the three entry points the barrier will call; `mxfs_v5_dlm_mount_settle` is now the residue retry only.

It also fixes something the old worker never did: `mount_stale_mask` is now narrowed to the fence-failure residue, so phase 3 has a well-defined retry set instead of re-walking slots already resolved.

**Behaviour is deliberately unchanged.** `mxfs_dlm_mount_recovery_settle` calls `settle_own_slot()` then `mount_settle()` back to back, reproducing 0.11.399 exactly. 0.11.400 therefore still carries the bootstrap deadlock and must not be boarded — the barrier call site is part 2.

**Design facts I verified along the way**, all recorded in ccmemory as `ccloop-c7ee71c6-sess56-step4a-barrier-api-split-landed` with the five remaining steps: `xfs_initialize_perag` at `xfs_mount.c:997` precedes `xfs_log_mount` at 1051, so the perag invalidation walk is legal at the insertion point; `xfs_log_mount_finish` (the first cluster-lock taker) is not until 1175; and upstream XFS itself refuses to `xfs_ail_push_all_sync` before recovery finishes (`xfs_log.c:868`) for the same reason GPT flagged — which is why the barrier's flush must be `mxfs_blkdev_flush_epoch` alone, not the peer-joined double round.

**Criteria: NO.** Not production ready. 11 open defects, 4 critical; defect #1's mount-ordering fix is half-landed and unverified, and no rig measurement was taken this session.

